            {
              "id": "II-002/likely-attack",
              "name": "II-002",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Tells the AI to hide what it is doing from the user"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Metadata instructs the model to conceal behaviour from the user."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Tells the AI to hide what it is doing from the user.\n\nLevel: Likely attack — A critical item, or a passage the AI reviewer judged malicious.\n\nWhat to do: Remove immediately. Concealment instructions have no legitimate use in tool metadata.\n\nFound by Faintprint's fixed rules (reference code II-002).\n\nEach server's full report, with the passage marked, is in the report folder: open index.html.",
                "markdown": "Tells the AI to hide what it is doing from the user.\n\n**Level:** Likely attack — A critical item, or a passage the AI reviewer judged malicious.\n\n**What to do:** Remove immediately. Concealment instructions have no legitimate use in tool metadata.\n\nFound by Faintprint's fixed rules (reference code II-002).\n\nEach server's full report, with the passage marked, is in the report folder: open index.html."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "mcp",
                  "supply-chain"
                ],
                "security-severity": "9.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "II-003/suspicious",
              "name": "II-003",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Instruction-style tags (such as <IMPORTANT>) in documentation"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Instruction-framing tag embedded in a documentation field."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Instruction-style tags (such as <IMPORTANT>) in documentation.\n\nLevel: Suspicious — A high-severity item, or a passage the AI reviewer judged suspicious.\n\nWhat to do: Strip pseudo-tags such as <IMPORTANT>; documentation fields must not simulate system framing.\n\nFound by Faintprint's fixed rules (reference code II-003).\n\nEach server's full report, with the passage marked, is in the report folder: open index.html.",
                "markdown": "Instruction-style tags (such as <IMPORTANT>) in documentation.\n\n**Level:** Suspicious — A high-severity item, or a passage the AI reviewer judged suspicious.\n\n**What to do:** Strip pseudo-tags such as <IMPORTANT>; documentation fields must not simulate system framing.\n\nFound by Faintprint's fixed rules (reference code II-003).\n\nEach server's full report, with the passage marked, is in the report folder: open index.html."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "security",
                  "mcp",
                  "supply-chain"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            }
          ]
